From: KB2UKA <kb2uka80@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dts): t8132: correct ANS mailbox IRQ roles

The ADT interrupt list is not ordered by the Linux mailbox role names.
On the J713, IRQ1005 is asserted while the receive FIFO is empty and
IRQ1006 is deasserted. Assigning 1005 to recv-not-empty makes the handler
repeatedly poll an empty FIFO before enable_irq() can return.

With only the receive pair exchanged, bounded RAM boots pass the
previously unreachable mailbox-start return and ANS boot-ready checkpoints.
The same idle-state capture shows IRQ1003 asserted for an empty send FIFO,
so also correct send-empty/send-not-empty to 1003/1004. A send-pair-only
follow-up preserves controller initialization but does not cure the later
Create Submission Queue timeout. Full-FIFO send recovery is not yet tested.
The SoC include affects every T8132 board; hardware validation is J713 only.
Do not generalize these IRQ numbers to other coprocessor mailboxes.

Credit: KB2UKA
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
@@ -958,8 +958,8 @@
 			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
-			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 1004 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
-			             <AIC_IRQ 1003 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
-			             <AIC_IRQ 1006 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
-			             <AIC_IRQ 1005 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 1003 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+			             <AIC_IRQ 1004 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+			             <AIC_IRQ 1005 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+			             <AIC_IRQ 1006 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 			interrupt-names = "send-empty", "send-not-empty",
 			                  "recv-empty", "recv-not-empty";
 			#mbox-cells = <0>;
